      <activity id="37c67d37-2fe3-5625-b441-984d935df443" activityNameId="929519f5-bd2f-5b57-8ed6-14c483cd9e25" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Process-specific burdens, inert material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Process-specific burdens, inert material landfill
landfill for inert, insoluble, largely unpolluted, mostly mineral wastes like bricks, concrete, excavation material with carbon content below 5%;
Synonyms: cleanfill; 
UUID: 2580da5d-07f8-4d11-bbbe-02f8f2c4487a
process-specific (i.e. independent of waste composition) energy demand and land use of landfill
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: 50% of the sites feature a base seal and leachate collection system. landfill with renaturation after closure. 
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: data from one literature source on sanitary landfill, adapted to features of this landfill type 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2580da5d-07f8-4d11-bbbe-02f8f2c4487a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
